  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday) \nIssued at 955 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nOn Saturday and Sunday, a narrow but amplified 5h ridge axis over the\nlower MO valley south into the western Gulf of America will be in\nplace, providing northerly flow aloft over the TN Valley. A sprawling\nsurface and 8h ridge will be in place from New England through the\nlower MS Valley. This will keep dry and seasonable weather in play\nthrough early next week. The ridge will break down Monday and \nTuesday as the southwest U.S. ejects into the Plains and OH Valley.\nThe southern tail of this wave will move through Tuesday into\nWednesday, but the airmass will too dry to support precipitation. \nThe surface ridge will remain in place, but pressures will be falling\nas it weakens. Temperatures in upper 60s to lower 70s on Monday \nunder the influence of the wedging ridge will warm into the lower to \nmiddle 70s Tuesday and Wednesday. Lows will be in the lower to middle\n40s over the weekend into Monday morning, warming into the middle \n40s to around 50 by Wednesday and Thursday mornings.",
